# The budget of each machine of the Podman lane that runs on the schedule and on a dispatch, and
# what it is made of. Nothing here is a guess: a test (tests/scripts/shell/podman_lane/lane-budget.test.sh)
# holds the matrix of .github/workflows/podman-lane.yml to this file, and holds this file to its own
# arithmetic:
#
#   vm_seconds  = ceil(measured_max_minutes x margin_percent / 100) minutes, in seconds
#   job_minutes = those minutes + overhead_minutes
#
# measured_max_minutes is the longest the VM took, from boot to the end of its work, in the run
# named below. margin_percent is not below 150. overhead_minutes is what the job spends outside the
# VM (the checkout, qemu and its tools, the image, the verification): at most 7.7 minutes in 20 runs
# measured on 2026-11-24, with three times that allowed.
#
# A VM cut at vm_seconds says `SLOW RUNNER` and the phase it had reached (verify-vm-log.sh). A cut
# once is a slow machine and the leg is run again. A cut every night is a measurement that is out of
# date: measure again (a dispatch of the lane prints the phases of each VM in its summary, one line
# each, by the VM's own clock), change the number here, and the workflow with it.
#
# leg       measured_max_minutes  margin_percent  vm_seconds  job_minutes
suite       49.4                  150             4500        100
coverage    68.9                  150             6240        129
#
# Where the numbers come from:
#   suite     the gating suite, the leak scan and the Quadlet generator tests of 301 tests: the phase
#             `suite-done` at 2960 s after boot, the boot step 49.5 minutes (the suite itself 2751.8 s);
#             the 15 scheduled runs before it, with 257 tests, took 2405 to 2484 s for the suite and 42.0
#             to 43.7 minutes to the summary. Run 45506283145 (a dispatch, 2026-11-24).
#   coverage  the instrumented run and its figure (90.67 %): `setup-done` at 63 s, `coverage-tool-installed`
#             at 135 s, `coverage-run-done` at 4123 s, the boot step 68.9 minutes. Same run.
# Before this the two shared one boot of 70 minutes, and the coverage was cut in every scheduled run
# (the VM lasted exactly 70.0 minutes in 15 of 15) and never produced a figure.
overhead_minutes 25
